x86_64-linux  the case keeps a static local on purpose - a static is one of the declarations [stmt.dcl]/3 lets a jump pass - and a static local's symbol is a recorded divergence: cxx1 names it function.variable where clang writes an _ZZ or ?s@?1?? name - see docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "A static local keeps its own name in the object file"
x86_64-windows  the case keeps a static local on purpose - a static is one of the declarations [stmt.dcl]/3 lets a jump pass - and a static local's symbol is a recorded divergence: cxx1 names it function.variable where clang writes an _ZZ or ?s@?1?? name - see docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "A static local keeps its own name in the object file"
